  "notes": "AAS in Surgical Technology 'Course Sequence by Term' as published on the official GateWay Community College Surgical Technology program page (Academic Plan Code 3673, Catalog Year 2026-2027, Effective Term Fall 2025), retrieved 2026-10-01. The page publishes two variants: Full-time (Fall/Spring/Summer core curriculum, Terms 1-5, sequenced here) and Introductory Courses Only (part-time). The Full-time variant covers the post-admission core curriculum; the following introductory courses must be completed with a 2.0 GPA before entering the core cohort and are sequenced in the part-time variant rather than the full-time variant: FYE101 or FYE103 (1-3), BIO201 (4), BIO202 (4), BIO205 (4), ENG101 or ENG107 (3), ENG102 or ENG108 (3), MAT150 or MAT151 or MAT152 or MAT155 or MAT156 (3-6), PHY101 (4), HCC/RES109 CPR for Health Care Provider (0-0.5, or proof of current AHA Health Care Provider CPR certification), HCC130 Fundamentals in Health Care Delivery (0-3, or permission of coordinator), HCC145 or HCC146 Medical Terminology (0-3, or work experience/equivalent). HCS154 (7 credits) is optional (for CRCST exam eligibility). Sequenced full-time sum = 59.5 (14+12.5+7+13+13) using maximum printed credit values for range cells, per the range convention; the catalog prints Total Credits Required 70.5-97. Students must earn a grade of C (defined as 75%) or better in all courses to successfully complete the program. Admission requires formal application, Level One Fingerprint Clearance, background check, and clinical health and safety compliance.",
